    <string name="adv_detection">Detection</string>
    <string name="adv_close_threshold">Close threshold</string>
    <string name="adv_close_threshold_help">Above this value, FlipLock considers the flap is not closed.</string>
    <string name="adv_min_drop">Minimum drop</string>
    <string name="adv_min_absolute_drop">Minimum absolute drop</string>
    <string name="adv_confirmation">Confirmation time</string>
    <string name="adv_cooldown">Cooldown</string>
    <string name="adv_min_baseline">Minimum usable baseline</string>
    <string name="adv_min_baseline_help">Below this ambient level, light alone cannot tell a dark room from a closed flap: FlipLock then refuses to lock (unless proximity confirms it).</string>

    <string name="adv_mode">Mode</string>
    <string name="adv_mode_help">AUTO: light decides when it is conclusive; proximity takes over only when the room is too dark and the sensor really produces events.</string>

    <string name="adv_background">Background reliability</string>
    <string name="adv_persistent_service">Persistent service</string>
    <string name="adv_persistent_service_help">Off by default. The accessibility service already watches the sensors, with no notification and no extra service.\n\nSwitch this on ONLY if TEST C fails, that is if closing the case does not lock the screen while FlipLock is not on screen. It adds a quiet notification that stops Android from cutting off sensors in the background.</string>

    <string name="adv_wake_title">Wake on open</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_unavailable">Automatic wake is not available on this device.</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_unavailable_help">No “wake-up” sensor able to wake the processor was found. The light sensor alone cannot do it while the screen is off.</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_switch">Turn the screen on when opening</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_threshold">Wake threshold</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_instant_window">Instant watch after locking</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_instant_disabled">off</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_instant_seconds">%1$d s</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_instant_help">During this window FlipLock listens to the light sensor directly: the screen comes back as soon as you open the flap, even with the phone still in your hand. This is the phase that covers “I close it then reopen it right away”.\n\nMeasured cost: keeping the processor out of suspend draws about 50 mW, roughly 0.004%% of the battery per lock for 60 s. The wake lock is partial (screen stays off) and expires on its own.</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_triggers_help">After that window, only the hardware wake-up triggers stay armed (about 0.001 mA):\n%1$s\n\nThey react to picking the phone up after it has been at rest; FlipLock then checks the light for at most 1.5 s.</string>
    <string name="adv_wake_limits">The screen turns on at the lock screen: your PIN, fingerprint or face is still required.\n\nLimits: in a completely dark room, opening the flap does not change the light level — the screen will not turn on. And the wake only arms if the screen went off while the flap was closed, so the phone does not light up by itself on a desk.</string>

